file     crates/credentials-module/tests/fixtures/enrollment_wire_contract.json
field    operations[op == "credential.list_scoped"].reply   (a string: the whole wire body)
copied   2026-09-22, via `git show bbd370f3:<file>`, CI green on that sha
history  96f2f476 carried `"type":"subscription"`, a value the producer never
         emits (hand-typed on their side); bbd370f3 computes `type` and
         `serves` from the producer's own catalog functions, and adds a second
         row so every optional key appears both present and absent.

The producer serialises its real ListScopedResult into that file and a test on
its side fails if the type's output stops matching it, so a change there fails
first in claustrum. To refresh: repeat the git show at the new sha, update this
file's sha, and run the decode tests here -- never edit the JSON by hand.
